<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Serampore College</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1818">1818</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serampore">Serampore</a> College is a college in Serampore, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, founded in 1818 by the Baptist missionaries William Carey, Joshua Marshman and William Ward. In 1827 the King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> granted it a charter to award degrees, and it still confers theology degrees on colleges across India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/serampore-college.jpg" alt="Serampore College" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: gangulybiswarup · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Serampore_College_-_Hooghly_2017-07-06_0840-0860.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
